# SUPERCOMPUTE — Cloudflare Pages headers
# Static export output (public/ -> out/ on build).
#
# CLOUDFLARE SYNTAX: headers only apply inside a path section. A block with no
# path line ("/*" or "/path") is silently ignored — the previous revision of this
# file was written that way, so none of it ever reached a browser. Everything in
# the /* section below is therefore in effect for the FIRST time. Treat it as a
# fresh rollout, not a tweak.
#
# COEP require-corp was declared in that dead block and is intentionally NOT
# re-added: it would block cross-origin images/media that lack CORP headers.
#
# CSP <-> transport invariant (kept honest in BOTH directions):
#   Browser-side RPC transports are defined in lib/web3.ts and every one of them
#   MUST be listed in connect-src below:
#     base    -> https://mainnet.base.org   (viem's Base default)
#     mainnet -> https://eth.drpc.org
#   Both are pinned explicitly in lib/web3.ts so this stays a static mapping. A
#   bare http() would resolve to chain.rpcUrls.default.http[0] at request time:
#   for mainnet that is https://eth.merkle.io, which 429s (Cloudflare error 1015)
#   under ordinary traffic, so mainnet is pinned to a host that answers reads.
#
#   The other mainnet RPC hosts in the repo (functions/api/auth.js,
#   functions/api/web3/[[catchall]].js, functions/api/token.js) are Cloudflare
#   Pages Functions: server-side, where CSP does not apply. They deliberately do
#   NOT appear here — listing a host the browser never contacts makes the policy
#   lie about its own trust surface, and none of them work from a browser anyway
#   (llamarpc/publicnode fail the TLS handshake, cloudflare-eth.com cannot serve
#   eth_blockNumber). Adding a browser-side read against any of them requires
#   adding it below first.
#
#   The subscriber funnel (/subscribe, /dashboard, paid rail) adds NO new
#   browser-side origin: wallet connect uses lib/web3.ts transports (listed),
#   SIWE auth and every subscriber call are same-origin /api/*, and EIP-3009
#   signing is local to the wallet. connect-src therefore stays exactly as-is.
#
# COOP: same-origin-allow-popups. A popup-based flow IS live — the Coinbase
# Wallet connector (lib/web3.ts) opens a popup that needs the opener
# relationship; under `same-origin` that popup loses window.opener. This value
# keeps COOP's cross-origin isolation for windows we do not open ourselves while
# restoring the opener for the ones we do. It does NOT affect extension wallets
# (MetaMask's popup is browser UI, not a page) and does NOT weaken the CSP.
#
# X-Frame-Options is SAMEORIGIN, aligned with frame-ancestors 'self'. It was DENY,
# which contradicted the CSP: modern browsers honour frame-ancestors and ignore
# XFO, older ones let DENY win — so same-origin framing silently broke on older
# browsers. SAMEORIGIN keeps the legacy clickjacking protection and agrees with
# the CSP instead of removing the header.
#
# CSP violation telemetry (card t_38a77267): the enforcing policy below reports
# every violation to /api/csp-report (Pages Function -> D1 table csp_reports),
# rolled up as a count per day|directive|origin|document. Read it with
# scripts/csp-report-stats.sh; see docs/csp-telemetry.md.
#   - Reporting-Endpoints / Report-To carry the ABSOLUTE prod URL, as specified.
#     On a preview branch (<branch>.supercompute.pages.dev) the legacy
#     `report-uri` fallback is document-relative and therefore stays on the
#     preview origin; only modern-Chrome (report-to) reports go to prod.
#   - The collector is same-origin and adds NO new browser-side origin, so
#     connect-src is unchanged by this addition.
#
# HSTS + expanded Permissions-Policy (F6 salvage from PR #70, recovered 2026-09-18):
#   HSTS: 1 year, includeSubDomains, NO preload (preload is a separate, deliberate
#   commitment). includeSubDomains was checked against every name resolving under
#   the zone: only supercompute.io / www / staging serve content; the rest are 522
#   (no origin behind them) or 404, identical over https. Any FUTURE subdomain
#   answering only plain HTTP will hard-fail in browsers that have seen this
#   header. Rollback is a one-line removal here plus Clear-HSTS in the CF
#   dashboard — never a preload.
#   Permissions-Policy payment=(), usb=(): verified unused before extending —
#   0 hits for PaymentRequest | canMakePayment | navigator.usb across the built
#   export and across lib/ components/ pages/ functions/. The fiat ramp
#   (components/FiatRamp.tsx) is a top-level window.open() — a separate document
#   this policy does not cover. A WebUSB hardware wallet would need usb=(self).
#
#   DROPPED FROM #70: it also carried `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin`.
#   That is deliberately NOT taken — main's `same-origin-allow-popups` (PR #94) is
#   newer and fixes popup wallet flows losing window.opener. Keeping #70's value
#   would have silently broken wallet connect.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.neynar.com https://fonts.gstatic.com https://mainnet.base.org https://eth.drpc.org https://*.walletconnect.com https://*.walletconnect.org wss://*.walletconnect.com wss://*.walletconnect.org; media-src 'self' blob: https:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' https://*.walletconnect.com https://*.walletconnect.org https://www.youtube.com https://calendly.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests; report-uri /api/csp-report; report-to csp
  Reporting-Endpoints: csp="https://supercompute.io/api/csp-report"
  Report-To: {"group":"csp","max_age":10886400,"endpoints":[{"url":"https://supercompute.io/api/csp-report"}]}
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Immutable hashed build assets
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# HTML — never cache stale
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# ENS resolver — read-only public resolver. Short browser cache, longer edge
# cache (the function itself caches in KV for 1h). No CORS header: every caller
# (lib/ens.ts) is same-origin, and a wildcard ACAO would advertise a
# cross-origin read surface that does not exist.
/api/ens/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=60, s-maxage=300
